cial Security tax  above 400,000 a year in earnings that  raises a huge amount of money from  people earning above $400,000 a year  Biden  would propose or proposes eliminating  the stepped-up basis provision for  inheritances I explained that last time  I mean this is really significant stuff  in terms of the money it would raise  I won't redo the entire tax segment but  needless to say many in the audience  appreciated it some just came in and  said it's not as progressive as what  Bernie wanted okay let's now look at Joe  Biden's proposal on environmental  justice and climate change and clean  energy now off the bat there's a bunch  of sort of regular regulatory stuff in  the proposal which I'm not going to  spend a lot of time on but it does bear  mentioning which includes Biden would  establish an environmental climate  justice division in the Department of  Justice Biden would make environmental  justice a priority within the federal  government Biden would refresh the way  that and sort of rehash the way that the  EPA does compliance that stuff deserves  attention but I want to look at some of  the specific metrics and actions that  Joe Biden is included in his plan so for  example Joe Biden includes specific  water quality improvements just to pick  one thing that's in his climate plan and  if you look at this part of the plan  Biden actually discusses and addresses  specific chemicals that are too much in  our drinking water and he does it in a  way where he sees water not only as an  environmental issue  which it is but also as an economic  issue which it is he sees water as an  issue of social justice as well so I  think we should all be pleased that Joe  Biden is talking about water quality in  his environmental proposal in a way that  shows understanding of how water relates  to race class geography economics etc  etc remember Joe Biden said that he  would use the green New Deal as a  framework in thinking about what he  wants to do and you can identify many  things in his climate change and clean  energy proposals that are almost  verbatim from the green New Deal now  what's hilarious is when Biden put this  out  and people identified look this is like  straight out of Bernie's plan this is  straight out of green New Deal  there were people who previously were  criticizing Biden for not being  progressive enough who now are saying oh  look Biden copied stuff from Bernie and  the green New Deal  shouldn't we be glad to see Biden  adopting things from Bernie Sanders and  from the green you deal like if the  concern was that Biden wasn't taking the  green New Deal seriously enough  shouldn't we be glad to see elements of  the green you deal in Biden's proposal  and you can see these components in a  few different areas when you look at  Biden's plan for retrofitting buildings  and schools in a way that will be good  for the environment but economically  stimulative that's straight out of the  green New Deal  a lot of the other things Biden includes  in these proposals are pretty obvious  things but there are things that aren't  being done or at least not done enough  like for example more seriously putting  in place subsidies and rebates when  Americans upgrade to more efficient  sources of energy and better windows and  efficient appliances that's worthwhile  government spending now two days ago  Donald Trump attacked Joe Biden for  having an ambitious goal in his proposal  and the goal is Biden wants to be carbon  to carbon pollution free electricity by  2035 meaning by 2035 Biden wants the  country to be generating electricity  from sources that do not pollute from  the standpoint of carbon that's a huge  task but if the criticism here is that  Biden is too ambitious on climate and  clean energy I'll take it I mean look at  the Trump administration that's going in  the opposite direction wanting to loosen  emission standards for vehicles wanting  to rehabilitate coal we've had that for  three and a half years I'l